primer-spec adoption of @bjornpagen/bumbledb 0.16.0 — the one-representation
release (bumbledb proposals/one-representation/, deletion ledger entries
D10/D11/D12; see primer-adoption.md alongside this file).

Base commit: d4f1efd0c98b13f6fecb1b4e2c3f2143274a2009
("Centralize every vendor model id in one seat registry.")

Apply from the primer-spec root:

    git apply primer-adoption.patch

D10 — the packing shim dies: runtime.ts's columnBatch/loadColumns/
loadBatchSize/isFactArray/isStringRecord/isCompleteColumnBatch and the
local ColumnBatch/CollectionWrite column arm; the oracle backend's
RelationColumnBatch/isRelationColumnBatch/loadColumns (renamed to `load`,
rows judged by the same isRelationFacts law as every other load); the
normalization witness writer's column buffers and 16_384 batch capacity.
The admit load becomes the plain nativeBuilder.load(relation, facts).
D11 — countRelations reads the engine's maintained exact count:
counts[name] = instance.count(relation), bigint, one lease, no scan.
D12 — vacuous at this commit: primer-spec carries no @ts-expect-error,
@ts-ignore, or biome-ignore anywhere in src/, scripts/, or packages/.

